    "summary": "High‑energy Oakland ’82 with historic Phil 6‑string debut and fiery China>Rider",
    "review": "December 26, 1982 at the Oakland Auditorium Arena captures a late‑‘82 Dead in full swing. The band rolls through a non‑standard setlist that drops an early Touch of Grey, a ripping Far From Me, and a high‑octane China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that many fans still talk about. Jerry is articulate on Eyes of the World and “goes off” in several spots, while Phil’s debut on a six‑string Modulus/Alembic bass adds a fresh low‑end punch that feels historic. The second set builds a tight groove through Throwing Stones, Wharf Rat and an uplifting Good Lovin’, closing with a playful encore of Keep Your Day Job. Musically the show is solidly in the “high‑energy ’82” vein – tight, bright, and full of those signature transitions, even if a few moments (notably the China/Rider segue on some tapes) feel a bit rushed.",
